  "notes": "USAGE:\nOften used in the ている form to describe a state of discoloration. The change is gradual and usually undesirable. Common for describing aging surfaces, tarnished metals, and stained materials.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {壁|かべ}が{黒|くろ}ずむ (a wall darkens)\n- {肌|はだ}が{黒|くろ}ずむ (skin becomes discolored)\n- {銀|ぎん}が{黒|くろ}ずむ (silver tarnishes)\n- {黒|くろ}ずんだ{汚|よご}れ (dark discoloration/stain)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {黒|くろ}くなる: to become black — a straightforward color change, while {黒|くろ}ずむ implies gradual darkening or discoloration\n- {汚|よご}れる: to get dirty — broader meaning; {黒|くろ}ずむ specifically refers to dark discoloration",
